trsp:att.6A439A6743
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "File Type Conversion Services"@en ;
  schema:category Transparency|Scope of Services|Value-Added|Crosswalks and Conversions|File Type Conversion Services ;
  skos:definition File Type Conversion Services encompass capabilities for identifying file formats using established registries (e.g., IANA MIME types, PRONOM), migrating obsolete formats to sustainable alternatives, and providing high-quality format conversion guidance. The repository publishes tools used for translation, transformation, or mediation between data formats, and discloses whether these tools operate within broader workflows such as ingestion or validation. ;
  owl:versionInfo 0.4 ;
  skos:inScheme trsp:trsp-attributes .


trsp:att.2141FF7751
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Flexible Serialisation of AIPs"@en ;
  schema:category Transparency|Scope of Services|Value-Added|Crosswalks and Conversions|Flexible Serialisation of AIPs ;
  skos:definition Flexible serialisation of AIPs refers to a system's ability to support multiple API serialisation methods and to document the technical standards and specifications governing all aspects of AIP packaging. As part of an exit strategy, the system enables batch export of information packages and associated metadata in a manageable format for ingest into another trusted digital archive. ;
  owl:versionInfo 0.4 ;
  skos:broader trsp:att.79D95E290A ;
  trsp:hasCardinalityType trsp:cardinality0_1 ;
  trsp:hasMeasurementType trsp:measurementTypeBinaryEvidence ;
  skos:inScheme trsp:trsp-attributes .


trsp:att.3B49F36F75
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Metadata Crosswalks Supported"@en ;
  schema:category Transparency|Scope of Services|Value-Added|Crosswalks and Conversions|Metadata Crosswalks Supported ;
  skos:definition A repository capability indicating support for mapping, transforming, and aligning metadata across different schemas, standards, or structural formats. The repository publishes a list of supported crosswalks, specifying schema pairs and their defined mappings to facilitate metadata schema compliance. Crosswalks are available both from and to the repository's supported metadata profiles. ;
  owl:versionInfo 0.4 ;
  skos:broader trsp:att.540F680A1E ;
  trsp:hasCardinalityType trsp:cardinality0_n ;
  trsp:hasMeasurementType trsp:measurementTypeBinaryEvidence ;
  skos:inScheme trsp:trsp-attributes .


trsp:att.6CA1A54238
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Package Crosswalks Supported"@en ;
  schema:category Transparency|Scope of Services|Value-Added|Crosswalks and Conversions|Package Crosswalks Supported ;
  skos:definition A capability indicating that the system supports access to and exchange of its Archival Information Packages (AIPs) using a defined protocol and set of APIs. These APIs are documented in both human- and machine-readable formats, enabling interoperability through package crosswalks and conversions. ;
  owl:versionInfo 0.4 ;
  skos:inScheme trsp:trsp-attributes .


trsp:att.699F35CDBC
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Quality-Assured Crosswalks"@en ;
  schema:category Transparency|Scope of Services|Value-Added|Crosswalks and Conversions|Quality-Assured Crosswalks ;
  skos:definition Quality-assured crosswalks are mappings between metadata schemas or classification systems that have been verified for semantic correctness. As a value-added service within the scope of crosswalks and conversions, this process ensures that conceptual equivalences between schemes are accurate and reliable. ;
  owl:versionInfo 0.4 ;
  skos:inScheme trsp:trsp-attributes .


